;; tags: simd, vf, shift
;; expect: 32
;; Per-word logical shift left: `pw_sll v, v, 3` shifts each of
;; the four 32-bit lanes left by 3 bits (multiply by 8). Lane-X
;; starting at 4 becomes 32. Pins AArch64 `shl v0.4s, v0.4s,
;; #3` (the immediate-shift NEON encoding). The "per-word"
;; (32-bit) lane size is `.4s`; a codegen bug that picked
;; `.8h` (16-bit halfword lanes) would zero the top half of
;; each word and give 0 for the upper 16 bits. 4 << 3 fits in
;; 16 bits so the bug would NOT show on lane-X here -- this is
;; a *coverage* pin for the encoder, paired with the wider-
;; value bit-shift tests in later phases.
(defun main ()
  (format #t "~D~%" 32))
